{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Live capture (2026-08-06, closing c827-2a23-cd00-473e from the loop-breaker checkout, main at 9a27202837): the primary completion-verifier run looped and was correctly aborted by the c827 actuator (requests=119, distinct_ratio_window=0.5). Bounded recovery started, but the evidence agent for ONE criterion hit its own step budget with a perfectly HEALTHY profile — 'completion-verifier-evidence ... hit step budget (request_limit=20 max_iterations=40) requests=20 tool_calls=35 distinct=35 max_consecutive_repeat=1 distinct_ratio_window=1.0 top_repeats=[]' — and that single LLMBudgetExhaustedError propagated out of the per-criterion loop in CompletionAgentStep._recover (completion_recovery.py ~:519-536), discarding all evidence already gathered and failing the whole recovery. The gate then reported 'bounded evidence recovery also failed' and offered --force-close: the exact exhaustion-is-not-a-verdict trap this cluster removes, one layer down.\n\nThe defect: the per-criterion evidence loop treats a single criterion's budget exhaustion as fatal to the aggregate, when the bound is a per-criterion safeguard. Partial evidence must be preserved rather than discarded — the finalizer already renders per-criterion verdicts and can mark a criterion unverifiable-within-bounds.\n\nPlan: catch LLMBudgetExhaustedError and RunawayToolLoopError around the per-criterion runner.run in _recover; substitute a content-free placeholder evidence entry that names the failure class and its usage counters (from the exception diagnostic), mark the entry exhausted=true; continue with remaining criteria; recovery fails outright only if EVERY criterion's evidence run fails. Placeholder text must never be presentable as affirmative evidence — it must state that evidence could not be gathered within recovery bounds so the finalizer scores the criterion unmet/indeterminate, not met. Aggregate char bound and finalizer input bound stay as-is. CompletionRecoveryError raised only when zero criteria produced evidence, carrying counts {criteria_total, criteria_exhausted}.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A single criterion's LLMBudgetExhaustedError no longer aborts recovery: with N criteria and one evidence run exhausting, the finalizer still runs and receives N evidence entries, the exhausted one carrying an explicit could-not-gather-within-bounds placeholder (unit test, held-out oracle style).\n- [ ] A RunawayToolLoopError raised by an evidence run is handled the same way (unit test).\n- [ ] The placeholder is content-free (no exception prose interpolated beyond the failure class name and numeric usage counters) and can never read as affirmative evidence (unit test asserts wording).\n- [ ] If EVERY criterion's evidence run fails, recovery raises CompletionRecoveryError with diagnostic {criteria_total, criteria_exhausted} (unit test).\n- [ ] Successful-evidence behaviour is byte-identical: runs where no evidence agent fails produce the same finalizer input as before (unit test).\n- [ ] Live Bedrock proof before ship: a real gate-style recovery over multiple criteria where at least one evidence run exhausts completes with a verdict instead of failing whole (session experiment, not in unit suite).\n- [ ] make lint and mypy clean; full CI marker suite matches the pre-existing baseline.\n\n## Testing\nHeld-out unit oracle in tests/unit/workflow/ (written before the fix, RED first): `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/ -q`. Mutation checks on the fix. Live Bedrock experiment (session artifact, not in unit suite) proving a multi-criterion recovery with one exhausted evidence run still reaches a verdict. `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean; full marker suite matches pre-existing baseline."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785984564436062001,"uuid":"59603ea2-53f4-4803-a178-3ca9eda13dc4"}